:CharacterString\u003e           \u003c/gmd:alternateTitle\u003e           \u003cgmd:identifier\u003e             \u003cgmd:MD_Identifier\u003e               \u003cgmd:code\u003e                 \u003cgco:CharacterString\u003eEXT_DS100758\u003c/gco:CharacterString\u003e               \u003c/gmd:code\u003e             \u003c/gmd:MD_Identifier\u003e           \u003c/gmd:identifier\u003e         \u003c/gmd:CI_Citation\u003e       \u003c/gmd:citation\u003e       \u003cgmd:abstract xsi:type\u003d\"gmd:PT_FreeText_PropertyType\"\u003e         \u003cgco:CharacterString\u003eThis is a GIS dataset owned by the Welsh Government and licensed to Natural Resources Wales (NRW) for internal use only.  In recognition of the different physical and socio-economic characteristics across the regions, the European Union introduced the Less Favoured Area (LFA) designation to support farming where production conditions are difficult. The criteria for LFA designation were first established in European legislation in 1975 (Directive 75/268 EEC and accompanying measures).\u003c/gco:CharacterString\u003e         \u003cgmd:PT_FreeText\u003e           \u003cgmd:textGroup\u003e             \u003cgmd:LocalisedCharacterString locale\u003d\"#EN\"\u003eThis is a GIS dataset owned by the Welsh Government and licensed to Natural Resources Wales (NRW) for internal use only.  In recognition of the different physical and socio-economic characteristics across the regions, the European Union introduced the Less Favoured Area (LFA) designation to support farming where production conditions are difficult. The criteria for LFA designation were first established in European legislation in 1975 (Directive 75/268 EEC and accompanying measures).\u003c/gmd:LocalisedCharacterString\u003e           \u003c/gmd:textGroup\u003e         \u003c/gmd:PT_FreeText\u003e       \u003c/gmd:abstract\u003e       \u003cgmd:pointOfContact\u003e         \u003cgmd:CI_ResponsibleParty\u003e           \u003cgmd:organisationName\u003e  